cess","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Key closure-risk indicators for a young '40 Act ETF:**\n\n**Seed capital**\n- **Seed size vs. AUM:** Is organic money above the seed? If seed is still most of AUM, the fund is fragile.\n- **Seed terms:** Seeders, often market makers, usually exit after 6–12 months. Watch for redemptions near that point.\n- **Concentration:** A few holders owning most shares means one exit can shrink the fund sharply.\n\n**Sponsor economics**\n- **Breakeven AUM:** Fixed costs (admin, custody, index licensing, listing, audit) are often $250k–$500k+ a year. At the expense ratio, many funds need roughly $25–50M to cover them.\n- **Fee waivers and expense caps:** Large or expiring waivers show the sponsor is subsidizing the fund.\n- **Sponsor health:** Watch the size of the lineup, past closures, and use of a white-label trust.\n- **Flow trend and liquidity:** Look at net creations, spreads, and volume.\n- **Distribution:** Check platform and model-portfolio placements.\n\nThese are signals, not predictions of closure.","ttft_ms":1480,"type":"result","duration_ms":5620,"uuid":"c48c9f75-f180-46d0-ae38-4ada318cc2c2","ttft_stream_ms":1251,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1251,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
